{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"issue 5946 marked duplicate July 2 2025 duplicate of #4588 rationale disposition temporary MultipartForm otelgin"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"However, this approach will also introduce additional side effects, for which there is currently no better solution.  \\n\\n**Impact:**  \\n\\nAssuming our middleware is wrapped in the following manner: `m1(m2(otel-middleware(m3(fn))))`,  \\n\\nwhere `m1` and `m2` internally implement operations such as `request.ParseMultipartForm(1)`. Due to the effect of `RemoveAll` in `otel-middleware`,  \\n\\nthere may be cases where they repeatedly create `request.MultipartForm` resources, resulting in additional memory allocations.\\n\\nOf course, we can also choose not to handle it, but we need to remind users to process `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`.\\n\\n----\\n\\nI'd like to hear your opinions: @akats7 @open-telemetry/go-approvers \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `area: instrumentation`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `bug`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `instrumentation: otelgin`\\n\\n- 2024-11-21T12:21:58Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/4588\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:45Z · **cross-referenced** by Yiling-J ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609\\n\\n- 2025-07-02T08:06:05Z · **marked_as_duplicate** by dmathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"howev this approach will also introduc addit side effect for which there is current no better solut impact assum our middlewar is wrap in the follow manner m1 m2 otel middlewar m3 fn where m1 and m2 intern implement oper such a request parsemultipartform 1 due to the effect of removeal in otel middlewar there may be case where they repeat creat request multipartform resourc result in addit memori alloc of cours we can also choos not to handl it but we need to remind user to process c request multipartform removeal i d like to hear your opinion akats7 open telemetri go approv sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston timelin 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx area instrument 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx bug 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx instrument otelgin 2024 11 21t12 21 58z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 4588 2025 01 13t13 45 45z cross referenc by yile j http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 2025 07 02t08 06 05z mark _ a _ duplic by dmathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"5b39be36d40588b5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.36028250718157306, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18870333883081872, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7606339, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Description\\n\\n Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed.\\n\\n### Environment\\n\\n- OS: MacOS\\n\\n- Architecture: x86\\n\\n- Go Version: 1.22\\n\\n- `otelgin` version: 0.53.0\\n\\n### Steps To Reproduce\\n\\n1. Using this code start up gin http server\\n\\n```\\n\\npackage main\\n\\nimport (\\n\\n\\t\\\"net/http\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"github.com/gin-gonic/gin\\\"\\n\\n\\t\\\"go.opentelemetry.io/contrib/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin\\\"\\n\\n)\\n\\nfunc main() {\\n\\n\\tengine := gin.Default()\\n\\n\\tengine.MaxMultipartMemory = 1024 * 1024\\n\\n\\tengine.Use(otelgin.Middleware(\\\"my-server\\\"))\\n\\n\\tengine.POST(\\\"/upload\\\", func(c *gin.Context) {\\n\\n\\t\\tff, err := c.FormFile(\\\"file\\\")\\n\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t_ = c.AbortWithError(http.StatusInternalServerError, err)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\treturn\\n\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t_ = ff\\n\\n\\t\\tc.JSON(http.StatusOK, map[string]interface{}{\\\"c\\\": 0})\\n\\n\\t})\\n\\n\\tengine.Run(\\\":8624\\\")\\n\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\n2. Upload a file to the http api\\n\\n```\\n\\ncurl --request POST \\\\\\n\\n  --url http://127.0.0.1:8624/upload \\\\\\n\\n  --header 'Content-Type: multipart/form-data' \\\\\\n\\n  --header 'User-Agent: insomnia/9.3.2' \\\\\\n\\n  --form 'file=@xxx.mp4'\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nUpload a file larger than MaxMultipartMemory, and the HTTP server will generate multipart-xxxx temporary files in the system temporary directory. These files will be automatically destroyed when the request ends. However, if the otelgin.Middleware is used, the temporary files will not be destroyed.  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston descript descript use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy environ o maco architectur x86 go version 1 22 otelgin version 0 53 0 step to reproduc 1 use this code start up gin http server packag main import net http github com gin gonic gin go opentelemetri io contrib instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin func main engin gin default engin maxmultipartmemori 1024 1024 engin use otelgin middlewar my server engin post upload func c gin context ff err c formfil file if err nil _ c abortwitherror http statusinternalservererror err return _ ff c json http statusok map string interfac c 0 engin run 8624 2 upload a file to the http api curl request post url http 127 001 8624 upload header content type multipart form data header user agent insomnia 93 2 form file xxx mp4 expect behavior upload a file larger than maxmultipartmemori and the http server will generat multipart xxxx temporari file in the system temporari directori these file will be automat destroy when the request end howev if the otelgin middlewar is use the temporari file will not be destroy\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"d99ea99e0323e3d0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32807488928420525, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15299610612029316, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73659205, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +95 / -0 across 3 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nFix #5946 \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +95 / -0 across 3 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (15)\\n\\n**linux-foundation-easycla[bot]** — 2025-01-13T13:45:52Z\\n\\n<a href=\\\"https://easycla.lfx.linuxfoundation.org/#/?version=2\\\"><img src=\\\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cla-project-logo-prod/cla-signed.svg?v=2\\\" alt=\\\"CLA Signed\\\" align=\\\"left\\\" height=\\\"28\\\" width=\\\"328\\\" ></a><br/><br />The committers listed above are authorized under a signed CLA.<ul><li>:white_check_mark: login: Yiling-J / name: Yiling-J  (b432f868ba452eb7a928e0b655fd1a2652b86ceb)</li></ul>\\n\\n---\\n\\n**codecov[bot]** — 2025-01-13T14:15:46Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main chang 95 0 across 3 file label mileston descript fix 5946 sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main chang 95 0 across 3 file label mileston discuss 15 linux foundat easycla bot 2025 01 13t13 45 52z a href http easycla lfx linuxfound org version 2 img src http s3 amazonaw com cla project logo prod cla sign svg v2 alt cla sign align left height 28 width 328 a br br the committ list abov are author under a sign cla ul li white _ check _ mark login yile j name yile j b432f868ba452eb7a928e0b655fd1a2652b86ceb li ul codecov bot 2025 01 13t14 15 46z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"d1ba8fa0c12fb484\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3159092883553414, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14662956907905914, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7108953, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-04]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479584781  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-16\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n*   Tyler Yahn\\n\\n*   Damien Mathieu\\n\\n*   Bryan Boreham\\n\\n*   David Ashpole\\n\\n*   Robert Pająk\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**1. otelgin Context Reversal in DataRace**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** raised an issue regarding context reversal in DataRace for otelgin. The context, stored within the otelgin struct, is reverted after middleware execution to prevent parent middlewares from accessing the span. However, Go routines spawned after a request might still need the span in their context. This discussion was based on [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014).\\n\\n*   Damien believes the current behavior is correct and that users should explicitly pass the current context to spawned Go routines. He cited the collector's pattern of passing context directly outside HTTP requests for processors and exporters as a good example.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** agreed, suggesting that passing necessary values like the span to spawned Go routines is the appropriate solution. He also mentioned OpenTelemetry's pattern of linking spans for asynchronous operations rather than making them child references.\\n\\n**2. otelgin Middleware and Temporary Multi-part Forms**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** brought up an issue where using middleware causes temporary multi-part forms not to be destroyed. This occurs because the instrumentation clones the HTTP request, but the multipart form is not duplicated, preventing proper cleanup. This issue is a historical one, manifesting in otelgin but potentially affecting virtually all HTTP-related middleware.\\n\\n*   References for this issue include:\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 04 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479584781 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z updat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 16 attende tyler yahn damien mathieu bryan boreham david ashpol robert paj ą k transcript 1 otelgin context revers in datarac damien mathieu rais an issu regard context revers in datarac for otelgin the context store within the otelgin struct is revert after middlewar execut to prevent parent middlewar from access the span howev go routin spawn after a request might still need the span in their context this discuss wa base on http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 damien belief the current behavior is correct and that user should explicit pas the current context to spawn go routin he cite the collector s pattern of pass context direct outsid http request for processor and export a a good exampl tyler yahn agre suggest that pass necessari valu like the span to spawn go routin is the appropri solut he also mention opentelemetri s pattern of link span for asynchron oper rather than make them child refer 2 otelgin middlewar and temporari multi part form damien mathieu brought up an issu where use middlewar caus temporari multi part form not to be destroy this occur becaus the instrument clone the http request but the multipart form is not duplic prevent proper cleanup this issu is a histor one manifest in otelgin but potenti affect virtual all http relat middlewar refer for this issu includ http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"d2762ef7a24b09d4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3121493883553414, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14662956907905916, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6983623, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:25\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"the HTTP server holds the original request, and using otelgin.Middleware replaces the request with [c.request = c.request.WithContext(ctx)](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/cb45b36c145ff13e4ba76fd9e02ef39297c906b5/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gintrace.go#L79), causing subsequent c.FormFile reads to fall on the new request. As a result, the original request held by the HTTP server does not have the MultipartForm, preventing it from being destroyed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (11)\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-01-11T11:28:03Z\\n\\n@akats7 Is there any plan to address this issue? For reference, a similar problem was resolved in Echo with this fix: [Echo-contrib PR #90](https://github.com/labstack/echo-contrib/pull/90/files#diff-86bf6c8ade26d5c58be942ac6765d89c8855c8713ba9a4d61249e16e3fa9c0fc).  If you're busy, I'd be happy to help by creating a PR to address it. Let me know!  \\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-01-12T13:54:25Z\\n\\ncc @akats7 as code owner.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-01-13T02:11:01Z\\n\\nHi @Yiling-J,\\n\\nFeel free to open a PR, I'll gladly review\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-07-02T08:35:01Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"the http server hold the origin request and use otelgin middlewar replac the request with c request c request withcontext ctx http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob cb45b36c145ff13e4ba76fd9e02ef39297c906b5 instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gintrac go l79 caus subsequ c formfil read to fall on the new request a a result the origin request held by the http server doe not have the multipartform prevent it from be destroy sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston discuss 11 yile j 2025 01 11t11 28 03z akats7 is there ani plan to address this issu for refer a similar problem wa resolv in echo with this fix echo contrib pr 90 http github com labstack echo contrib pull 90 file diff 86bf6c8ade26d5c58be942ac6765d89c8855c8713ba9a4d61249e16e3fa9c0fc if you re busi i d be happi to help by creat a pr to address it let me know dmathieu 2025 01 12t13 54 25z cc akats7 a code owner akats7 2025 01 13t02 11 01z hi yile j feel free to open a pr i ll glad review flc1125 2025 07 02t08 35 01z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"35baa43d7c471818\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3059959570988732, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11731351014124734, \"vector_similarity\": 0.746255, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I don’t think this is the expected result; in any case—whether it’s middleware or something else—it should be able to retrieve the file again.\\n\\nI think we may need to investigate this issue further.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\nBased on this PR, I’ve provided a prototype reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\\n@dmathieu @akats7, take a look and see how it works if we adjust it according to the prototype.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n@flc1125 can you clarify which behavior you’re referring to as incorrect, are you referring to \\n\\n```\\n\\nrequire.ErrorIs(t, err, fs.ErrNotExist)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\nI thought we had already agreed on the `RemoveAll` approach? Naturally, if you call RemoveAll, the temporary files are deleted and can’t be accessed afterward. Since this happens during the middleware’s return phase, I’d expect that most middlewares wouldn’t read the multipart form at that point anyway. I’m not sure if the implications of RemoveAll were discussed in the SIG meeting, but it might be worth confirming.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n@flc1125 I’m still not clear on the result you’re referring to, the result aligns to my understanding of what we’ve discussed.\\n\\nAlso I’m not sure if your prototype fix would work, I think it still doesn’t address the core issue which is that when we originally set c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx) with an unparsed form the http server won’t know to clean it up. I don’t think Cloning the request solves that.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t think this is the expect result in ani case whether it s middlewar or someth els it should be abl to retriev the file again i think we may need to investig this issu further flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 59 33z base on this pr i ve provid a prototyp refer http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161 dmathieu akats7 take a look and see how it work if we adjust it accord to the prototyp akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t15 42 57z flc1125 can you clarifi which behavior you re refer to a incorrect are you refer to requir errori t err f errnotexist yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t01 28 14z i thought we had alreadi agre on the removeal approach natur if you call removeal the temporari file are delet and can t be access afterward sinc this happen dure the middlewar s return phase i d expect that most middlewar wouldn t read the multipart form at that point anyway i m not sure if the implic of removeal were discuss in the sig meet but it might be worth confirm akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t10 24 52z flc1125 i m still not clear on the result you re refer to the result align to my understand of what we ve discuss also i m not sure if your prototyp fix would work i think it still doesn t address the core issu which is that when we origin set c request c request withcontext ctx with an unpars form the http server won t know to clean it up i don t think clone the request solv that sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"ee5caba072c6dc26\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28437836444708364, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09685597778154807, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7219306, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:43:31Z\\n\\nJust found an open 2 year old issue this would fix #4588 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:56:41Z\\n\\nThanks for the quick response @flc1125 , but I would like to offer a rebuttal. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## This PR Fixes an Existing Bug, Not Introducing New Safety Mechanisms\\n\\nI respectfully disagree with the characterization that this PR \\\"introduces mechanisms for concurrency safety.\\\" The opposite is true: this PR removes problematic code that causes a data race.\\n\\nThe current code has a real, reproducible race condition reported in issue #4588 (open for 2 years). The race detector fails consistently. This is not theoretical—it violates Go's memory model.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 43 31z just found an open 2 year old issu this would fix 4588 nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 56 41z thank for the quick respons flc1125 but i would like to offer a rebutt sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston this pr fix an exist bug not introduc new safeti mechan i respect disagre with the character that this pr introduc mechan for concurr safeti the opposit is true this pr remov problemat code that caus a data race the current code ha a real reproduc race condit report in issu 4588 open for 2 year the race detector fail consist this is not theoret it violat go s memori model sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"79dd2c776e5b2e7f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28417952778215855, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10843034683165509, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69426095, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:36: File removed: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n```\\n\\n----\\n\\nCurrently, I cannot determine whether this is a flaw in Go itself or if users are required to manually execute `RemoveAll()`. I have tried submitting [this issue](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455) to the official Go team to see if there will be any updates.\\n\\nThe following situations exist (tested and confirmed):\\n\\n1. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, but did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will be unable to delete the files;\\n\\n2. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, and manually called `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files;\\n\\n3. We executed `request.WithContext()` after executing `request.ParseMultipartForm,` and did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-07-03T13:24:52Z\\n\\nGiven that this [issue](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946#issuecomment-3028290240) currently lacks an official solution from the [Go team](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455), we need to find an appropriate workaround ourselves.\\n\\nMy suggestion is to proceed with the solution proposed in this [PR](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609) (also the consistent approach suggested by @zihuyishi and @akats7).  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 36 file remov var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 current i can not determin whether this is a flaw in go itself or if user are requir to manual execut removeal i have tri submit this issu http github com golang go issu 74455 to the offici go team to see if there will be ani updat the follow situat exist test and confirm 1 we execut request withcontext befor execut request parsemultipartform but did not manual call removeal on the new request it will be unabl to delet the file 2 we execut request withcontext befor execut request parsemultipartform and manual call removeal on the new request it will delet the file 3 we execut request withcontext after execut request parsemultipartform and did not manual call removeal on the new request it will delet the file flc1125 2025 07 03t13 24 52z given that this issu http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 issuecom 3028290240 current lack an offici solut from the go team http github com golang go issu 74455 we need to find an appropri workaround ourselv my suggest is to proceed with the solut propos in this pr http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 also the consist approach suggest by zihuyishi and akats7\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"5af8802d20a0e988\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28364407092443095, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09569727274918706, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7221866, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"=== RUN   TestIssue_Middleware\\n\\n    issue_test.go:55: req0.0: 0x140001b6500, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:15: req1.0: 0x140001b6500, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:20: req2.0: 0x140001b6500, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:30: req2.1: 0x140001b6640, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:34: req2.2: 0x140