ub.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T15:27:41Z\\n\\nThe goal of the test is to ensure that temporary files are automatically removed, not to test multipart file parsing. The sole purpose of using `c.FormFile` is to trigger multipart parsing, which creates temporary files. I added a `fileHeader.Open()` test in this function to confirm that the temporary file is available. However, I think checking the value of `ff` is unnecessary.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"flc1125 comment 2025 11 11t13 20 30z flc1125 comment 2025 11 11t13 59 33z akats7 comment 2025 11 11t15 42 57z yile j comment 2025 11 12t01 28 14z akats7 comment 2025 11 12t10 24 52z sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main chang 95 0 across 3 file label mileston review comment 28 flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t14 56 36z i believ the content of ff can be detect here flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t14 59 10z assert noerror flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t15 02 32z i m wonder if there s anoth middlewar layer outsid this one would it be remov becaus of this yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t15 27 41z the goal of the test is to ensur that temporari file are automat remov not to test multipart file pars the sole purpos of use c formfil is to trigger multipart pars which creat temporari file i ad a filehead open test in this function to confirm that the temporari file is avail howev i think check the valu of ff is unnecessari\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"05841978e5499c27\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.304343145595845, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10969303370835005, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75852674, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I don’t think this is the expected result; in any case—whether it’s middleware or something else—it should be able to retrieve the file again.\\n\\nI think we may need to investigate this issue further.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\nBased on this PR, I’ve provided a prototype reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\\n@dmathieu @akats7, take a look and see how it works if we adjust it according to the prototype.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n@flc1125 can you clarify which behavior you’re referring to as incorrect, are you referring to \\n\\n```\\n\\nrequire.ErrorIs(t, err, fs.ErrNotExist)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\nI thought we had already agreed on the `RemoveAll` approach? Naturally, if you call RemoveAll, the temporary files are deleted and can’t be accessed afterward. Since this happens during the middleware’s return phase, I’d expect that most middlewares wouldn’t read the multipart form at that point anyway. I’m not sure if the implications of RemoveAll were discussed in the SIG meeting, but it might be worth confirming.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n@flc1125 I’m still not clear on the result you’re referring to, the result aligns to my understanding of what we’ve discussed.\\n\\nAlso I’m not sure if your prototype fix would work, I think it still doesn’t address the core issue which is that when we originally set c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx) with an unparsed form the http server won’t know to clean it up. I don’t think Cloning the request solves that.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t think this is the expect result in ani case whether it s middlewar or someth els it should be abl to retriev the file again i think we may need to investig this issu further flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 59 33z base on this pr i ve provid a prototyp refer http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161 dmathieu akats7 take a look and see how it work if we adjust it accord to the prototyp akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t15 42 57z flc1125 can you clarifi which behavior you re refer to a incorrect are you refer to requir errori t err f errnotexist yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t01 28 14z i thought we had alreadi agre on the removeal approach natur if you call removeal the temporari file are delet and can t be access afterward sinc this happen dure the middlewar s return phase i d expect that most middlewar wouldn t read the multipart form at that point anyway i m not sure if the implic of removeal were discuss in the sig meet but it might be worth confirm akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t10 24 52z flc1125 i m still not clear on the result you re refer to the result align to my understand of what we ve discuss also i m not sure if your prototyp fix would work i think it still doesn t address the core issu which is that when we origin set c request c request withcontext ctx with an unpars form the http server won t know to clean it up i don t think clone the request solv that sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"ee5caba072c6dc26\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30203091105553503, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10534243007933573, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7609707, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"source