 remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main chang 95 0 across 3 file label mileston discuss 15 linux foundat easycla bot 2025 01 13t13 45 52z a href http easycla lfx linuxfound org version 2 img src http s3 amazonaw com cla project logo prod cla sign svg v2 alt cla sign align left height 28 width 328 a br br the committ list abov are author under a sign cla ul li white _ check _ mark login yile j name yile j b432f868ba452eb7a928e0b655fd1a2652b86ceb li ul codecov bot 2025 01 13t14 15 46z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"d1ba8fa0c12fb484\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2987885634346049, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0922906191922928, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7806171, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"We should also decide whether to fix this in otelgin only, or to review other middlewares and address the issue there as well if it exists.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-04T00:35:28Z\\n\\n> let’s reach an agreement on how we should fix it\\n\\nWe tend to only need to add the following on the basis of the original main branch:\\n\\n```go\\n\\nc.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()\\n\\n```\\n\\n> We should also decide whether to fix this in otelgin only, or to review other middlewares and address the issue there as well if it exists.\\n\\nIn fact, all middleware based on `*http.Request` has issues whenever a situation like `c.Request.WithContext(c.Request.Context())` occurs, so other components also need to be fixed.\\n\\nHowever, for this current PR, we only need to fix otelgin to keep the PR as minimal as possible. For other middleware, if you are interested, you can also submit fixes in the form of minimal PRs for individual components.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-04T01:19:00Z\\n\\n@flc1125 `RemoveAll()` works for me. I think my original PR already aligns well with the goal, it looks like I just need to resolve the conflicts and make sure the tests pass. Let me confirm agin that we’re all in agreement on this approach. @dmathieu @akats7\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T01:45:42Z\\n\\nSorry just got caught up on this thread. My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data. \\n\\nWhat about making it configurable with an Option, with the default behavior being to clean it up. That way the user can have more control over which middleware cleans up the form data.\\n\\nI don't want to stall this issue further but just a thought.\\n\\ncc. @flc1125 @dmathieu  \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T01:53:34Z\\n\\n> Sorry just got caught up on this thread. My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nAgree.\\n\\n> What about making it configurable with an Option, with the default behavior being to clean it up. That way the user can have more control over which middleware cleans up the form data.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"we should also decid whether to fix this in otelgin onli or to review other middlewar and address the issu there a well if it exist flc1125 2025 11 04t00 35 28z let s reach an agreement on how we should fix it we tend to onli need to add the follow on the basi of the origin main branch go c request multipartform removeal we should also decid whether to fix this in otelgin onli or to review other middlewar and address the issu there a well if it exist in fact all middlewar base on http request ha issu whenev a situat like c request withcontext c request context occur so other compon also need to be fix howev for this current pr we onli need to fix otelgin to keep the pr a minim a possibl for other middlewar if you are interest you can also submit fix in the form of minim pr for individu compon yile j 2025 11 04t01 19 00z flc1125 removeal work for me i think my origin pr alreadi align well with the goal it look like i just need to resolv the conflict and make sure the test pas let me confirm agin that we re all in agreement on this approach dmathieu akats7 akats7 2025 11 10t01 45 42z sorri just got caught up on this thread my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data i don t want to stall this issu further but just a thought cc flc1125 dmathieu flc1125 2025 11 10t01 53 34z sorri just got caught up on this thread my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data agre what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"3c8bf7e7b452e3f2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28911545597491495, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0966412228213071, \"vector_similarity\": 0.738222, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"```\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T08:21:31Z\\n\\nWouldn't we be fixing this rather more easily with the following:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\tc.Request = c.Request.Clone(ctx)\\n\\n```\\n\\n[WithContext](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.WithContext) performs a shallow clone, and therefore doesn't clone the multipart form.\\n\\nHowever, [Clone](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.Clone) performs a deep copy, and makes an explicit clone of [MultipartForm](https://cs.opensource.google/go/go/+/refs/tags/go1.23.4:src/net/http/request.go;l=406).\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:39:53Z\\n\\nThe problem here is, go http request will call MultipartForm.RemoveAll() automatically when request finishes. However, the otelgin middleware creates a new request, and temporary files will be stored in this new request's MultipartForm field. Unfortunately, no one is calling MultipartForm.RemoveAll() on this new request.\\n\\nA deep clone wouldn’t resolve the problem because the MultipartForm is also copied. A shallow clone might seem like it should work since the MultipartForm field is shared, but it doesn’t. This is because the MultipartForm field is lazily initialized—it’s only assigned a value when you [parse the form](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d/src/net/http/request.go#L1403). As a result, in the middleware, the field is nil.\\n\\nRelated issues: https://github.com/golang/go/issues/58809, https://github.com/labstack/echo/issues/2413\\n\\nI think other OpenTelemetry middlewares, such as otelmux and otelehco, might also have the same issue.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:55:45Z\\n\\nWhat if we parse the form before making the new request?\\n\\nWouldn't we share the object then?\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T15:31:10Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t08 21 31z wouldn t we be fix this rather more easili with the follow suggest c request c request clone ctx withcontext http pkg go dev net http request withcontext perform a shallow clone and therefor doesn t clone the multipart form howev clone http pkg go dev net http request clone perform a deep copi and make an explicit clone of multipartform http c opensourc googl go go ref tag go1 23 4 src net http request go l 406 yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 39 53z the problem here is go http request will call multipartform removeal automat when request finish howev the otelgin middlewar creat a new request and temporari file will be store in this new request s multipartform field unfortun no one is call multipartform removeal on this new request a deep clone wouldn t resolv the problem becaus the multipartform is also copi a shallow clone might seem like it should work sinc the multipartform field is share but it doesn t this is becaus the multipartform field is lazili initi it s onli assign a valu when you pars the form http github com golang go blob 6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d src net http request go l1403 a a result in the middlewar the field is nil relat issu http github com golang go issu 58809 http github com labstack echo issu 2413 i think other opentelemetri middlewar such a otelmux and otelehco might also have the same issu dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 55 45z what if we pars the form befor make the new request wouldn t we share the object then yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t15 31 10z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"0b66ff59ca7469a0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27617729089429494, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08794001556327848, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7153976, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I think this approach could work, but it feels a bit unusual to enforce form parsing in the middleware.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T16:18:27Z\\n\\nHaving to force remove multipart files is a bit unusual too.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:44:13Z\\n\\nI'm probably more in favor of doing the initialization on the original request as well, explicitly handling clean up logic does seem a bit strange\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:49:47Z\\n\\n@dmathieu maybe we should discuss this in the SIG since it might have implications in the other instrumentation modules\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:50:46Z\\n\\nI won't be able to attend this week's meeting (it's the week where it's late for EU). But yes, feel free to bring it there.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-19T18:17:34Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J what are you thoughts on parsing the form in the middleware, the more I think about it, the more that seems to be the better approach, for example what about certain edge cases where down the chain middlewares might want to access the files\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-20T01:52:04Z\\n\\n@akats7 Another option is to save `c.Request` to a variable before calling `c.Request.WithContext(ctx)`. Then, in the defer function, if `c.Request.MultipartForm != nil`, we can reattach the `MultipartForm` to the original request. This way, there won’t be any automatic removing or parsing. If other middlewares handle the form correctly, this approach should work. \\n\\nIn [http/server.go](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41/src/net/http/server.go#L2102), the `ServeHTTP` method is called first, which invokes the Gin handlers/middlewares, and then `finishRequest` is called, which removes the temporary files.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i think this approach could work but it feel a bit unusu to enforc form pars in the middlewar dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t16 18 27z have to forc remov multipart file is a bit unusu too akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 44 13z i m probabl more in favor of do the initi on the origin request a well explicit handl clean up logic doe seem a bit strang akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 49 47z dmathieu mayb we should discus this in the sig sinc it might have implic in the other instrument modul dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 50 46z i won t be abl to attend this week s meet it s the week where it s late for eu but yes feel free to bring it there akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 19t18 17 34z yile j what are you thought on pars the form in the middlewar the more i think about it the more that seem to be the better approach for exampl what about certain edg case where down the chain middlewar might want to access the file yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 20t01 52 04z akats7 anoth option is to save c request to a variabl befor call c request withcontext ctx then in the defer function if c request multipartform nil we can reattach the multipartform to the origin request this way there won t be ani automat remov or pars if other middlewar handl the form correct this approach should work in http server go http github com golang go blob 40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41 src net http server go l2102 the servehttp method is call first which invok the gin handler middlewar and then finishrequest is call which remov the temporari file\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"b3dbc649c958ce01\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2749267708942949, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08794001556327848, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7112292, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T15:31:16Z\\n\\nI prefer using `require.NoError` because it ensures that no additional information distracts me when a test has already failed. I also searched the codebase and seems that both `require` and `assert` are used, and `require.NoError` appears more.\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T15:35:44Z\\n\\nIt's hard to say, but in all cases, regardless of how many middlewares are chained, temporary files should be removed. I didn't check the return error of `RemoveAll` here, which aligns with the behavior in both Go's [`http` package](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/44a6f817ea0fbeb3ba4aa398794c4e80dba13b1e/src/net/http/server.go#L1727) and [echo-contrib](https://github.com/labstack/echo-contrib/pull/90). I believe each middleware should independently attempt to remove temporary files.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T16:20:13Z\\n\\nsee: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609#issuecomment-2587572600\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gintrace.go` — 2025-01-14T08:12:17Z\\n\\nRather than ignoring an error here, how about passing it to the otel error handler?\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\terr := c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\totel.Handle(err)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n```\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-14T08:13:50Z\\n\\nI think what @flc1125 meant here is that you don't necessarily need to use `AbortWithError` (which also can return an error but ignores it), but instead call `require.NoError` here.\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\trequire.NoError(err)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t15 31 16z i prefer use requir noerror becaus it ensur that no addit inform distract me when a test ha alreadi fail i also search the codebas and seem that both requir and assert are use and requir noerror appear more yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t15 35 44z it s hard to say but in all case regardless of how mani middlewar are chain temporari file should be remov i didn t check the return error of removeal here which align with the behavior in both go s http packag http github com golang go blob 44a6f817ea0fbeb3ba4aa398794c4e80dba13b1e src net http server go l1727 and echo contrib http github com labstack echo contrib pull 90 i believ each middlewar should independ attempt to remov temporari file flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t16 20 13z see http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 issuecom 2587572600 dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gintrac go 2025 01 14t08 12 17z rather than ignor an error here how about pass it to the otel error handler suggest err c request multipartform removeal if err nil otel handl err dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 14t08 13 50z i think what flc1125 meant here is that you don t necessarili need to use abortwitherror which also can return an error but ignor it but instead call requir noerror here suggest requir noerror err\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"a6289f2135157364\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27459165589429496, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08794001556327848, \"vector_similarity\": 0.71011215, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455)\\n\\n*   **Bryan Boreham** questioned the relevance to OpenTelemetry, to which Damien clarified it's for instrumenting file uploads via the HTTP server.\\n\\n*   The discussion revolved around implementing an automatic cleanup mechanism for these temporary files. Proposed solutions included:\\n\\n    *   Option 1: `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`\\n\\n    *   Option 2: Leave it to the user to decide (\\\"whoever uses it is responsible for cleanup\\\")\\n\\n    *   Option 3: Provide a configurable option with a default.\\n\\n*   Damien suggested starting with automatic deletion without an explicit option, adding one only if a strong need arises. The notes from the agenda suggested starting with default behavior of removal, waiting for user interest to add configuration, and empowering component owners to make this decision.\\n\\n*   Tyler acknowledged that the instrumentation is responsible for cleanup and that this issue needs to be addressed.\\n\\n**3. Long-seen Code Owners/Triagers Check-in**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** reported that Chengzhen (Scorpion Knives), a triager and code owner for otelzap and otelecho, has had no GitHub activity since February and is the sole owner for otelecho.\\n\\n*   Damien pinged Chengzhen on Slack today and will wait a couple of weeks for a response. If there's no response, he plans to propose moving Chengzhen to Emeritus status due to inactivity.\\n\\n**4. Robert Pająk's PR (Parsing Algorithm)**\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** asked Tyler if his PR ([sdk/log: Fix AddAttributes, SetAttributes, SetBody on Record to not mutate input #7403](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7403)) needed Tyler's specific review or if another approval would suffice to unblock it.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** encouraged others to review and stated that the project shouldn't be blocked waiting for him, though he would try to review it within a few days.\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** offered to review the PR. The goal is to merge it into the current milestone.\\n\\n**5. David Ashpole's PRs (Metrics SDK Optimizations)**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** provided an update on his histogram reservoir optimization PR. He explained that fixing a race condition initially worsened performance, making it equivalent to using a lock. The new approach involves one lock per measurement instead of one for the whole reservoir, resulting in a 3x-4x performance improvement. The PR is now much simpler and mostly involves concurrent safety testing.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 74455 http github com golang go issu 74455 bryan boreham question the relev to opentelemetri to which damien clarifi it s for instrument file upload via the http server the discuss revolv around implement an automat cleanup mechan for these temporari file propos solut includ option 1 c request multipartform removeal option 2 leav it to the user to decid whoever us it is respons for cleanup option 3 provid a configur option with a default damien suggest start with automat delet without an explicit option ad one onli if a strong need aris the note from the agenda suggest start with default behavior of remov wait for user interest to add configur and empow compon owner to make this decis tyler acknowledg that the instrument is respons for cleanup and that this issu need to be address 3 long seen code owner triager check in damien mathieu report that chengzhen scorpion knife a triager and code owner for otelzap and otelecho ha had no github activ sinc februari and is the sole owner for otelecho damien ping chengzhen on slack today and will wait a coupl of week for a respons if there s no respons he plan to propos move chengzhen to emeritus status due to inact 4 robert paj ą k s pr pars algorithm robert paj ą k ask tyler if his pr sdk log fix addattribut setattribut setbodi on record to not mutat input 7403 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7403 need tyler s specif review or if anoth approv would suffic to unblock it tyler yahn encourag other to review and state that the project shouldn t be block wait for him though he would tri to review it within a few day david ashpol offer to review the pr the goal is to merg it into the current mileston 5 david ashpol s pr metric sdk optim david ashpol provid an updat on his histogram reservoir optim pr he explain that fix a race condit initi worsen perform make it equival to use a lock the new approach involv one lock per measur instead of one for the whole reservoir result in a 3x 4x perform improv the pr is now much simpler and most involv concurr safeti test\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"88ce72df6cb6f6c4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2742408660409679, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09136267720138276, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70095664, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:25\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"pull request 6609 checks review approval merge status conflicts temporary multipart form otelgin\", \"similarity_thresho