etry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"8a1254612e6e6337\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33275325498597275, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20057996426567534, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6411576, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**svrnm** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-20T18:33:12Z\\n\\n**svrnm** — APPROVED — 2025-11-20T19:18:34Z\\n\\n**trask** — APPROVED — 2025-11-20T19:24:07Z\\n\\n**maryliag** — APPROVED — 2025-11-20T20:54:14Z\\n\\n**mx-psi** — APPROVED — 2025-11-21T10:32:49Z\\n\\n**jack-berg** — APPROVED — 2025-11-21T15:57:47Z\\n\\n**tedsuo** — APPROVED — 2025-12-01T18:24:54Z\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-02]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Project Proposal: Ecosystem Explorer (open-telemetry/community#3000)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000  \\n\\n**Author**: jaydeluca  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-09-19T10:11:57Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-02T08:40:24Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-01T19:04:18Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `instrumentation-docs` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +251 / -0 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: area/project-proposal  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Review Comments (13)\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T11:58:43Z\\n\\nPersonally I would put the extraction and availability of the meta data first, and the web application second. There might be other places&tools where people would want to have that data available.\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T11:59:42Z\\n\\neven if it would be a small one, I think having a dedicated SIG which is populated from Java&Comms and some other SIGs would be the way forward, and provide clear ownership.\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T11:59:55Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"svrnm comment 2025 11 20t18 33 12z svrnm approv 2025 11 20t19 18 34z trask approv 2025 11 20t19 24 07z maryliag approv 2025 11 20t20 54 14z mx psi approv 2025 11 21t10 32 49z jack berg approv 2025 11 21t15 57 47z tedsuo approv 2025 12 01t18 24 54z sourc id src pr 02 pull request project propos ecosystem explor open telemetri communiti 3000 canon url http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 author jaydeluca creat 2025 09 19t10 11 57z updat 2025 12 02t08 40 24z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 01t19 04 18z branch instrument doc main chang 251 0 across 2 file label area project propos mileston review comment 13 svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t11 58 43z person i would put the extract and avail of the meta data first and the web applic second there might be other place tool where peopl would want to have that data avail svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t11 59 42z even if it would be a small one i think have a dedic sig which is popul from java comm and some other sig would be the way forward and provid clear ownership svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t11 59 55z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"d1c12561e10f79e0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3275479792909484, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20044388470135494, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6241242, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-04]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479584781  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-16\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n*   Tyler Yahn\\n\\n*   Damien Mathieu\\n\\n*   Bryan Boreham\\n\\n*   David Ashpole\\n\\n*   Robert Pająk\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**1. otelgin Context Reversal in DataRace**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** raised an issue regarding context reversal in DataRace for otelgin. The context, stored within the otelgin struct, is reverted after middleware execution to prevent parent middlewares from accessing the span. However, Go routines spawned after a request might still need the span in their context. This discussion was based on [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014).\\n\\n*   Damien believes the current behavior is correct and that users should explicitly pass the current context to spawned Go routines. He cited the collector's pattern of passing context directly outside HTTP requests for processors and exporters as a good example.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** agreed, suggesting that passing necessary values like the span to spawned Go routines is the appropriate solution. He also mentioned OpenTelemetry's pattern of linking spans for asynchronous operations rather than making them child references.\\n\\n**2. otelgin Middleware and Temporary Multi-part Forms**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** brought up an issue where using middleware causes temporary multi-part forms not to be destroyed. This occurs because the instrumentation clones the HTTP request, but the multipart form is not duplicated, preventing proper cleanup. This issue is a historical one, manifesting in otelgin but potentially affecting virtually all HTTP-related middleware.\\n\\n*   References for this issue include:\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 04 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479584781 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z updat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 16 attende tyler yahn damien mathieu bryan boreham david ashpol robert paj ą k transcript 1 otelgin context revers in datarac damien mathieu rais an issu regard context revers in datarac for otelgin the context store within the otelgin struct is revert after middlewar execut to prevent parent middlewar from access the span howev go routin spawn after a request might still need the span in their context this discuss wa base on http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 damien belief the current behavior is correct and that user should explicit pas the current context to spawn go routin he cite the collector s pattern of pass context direct outsid http request for processor and export a a good exampl tyler yahn agre suggest that pass necessari valu like the span to spawn go routin is the appropri solut he also mention opentelemetri s pattern of link span for asynchron oper rather than make them child refer 2 otelgin middlewar and temporari multi part form damien mathieu brought up an issu where use middlewar caus temporari multi part form not to be destroy this occur becaus the instrument clone the http request but the multipart form is not duplic prevent proper cleanup this issu is a histor one manifest in otelgin but potenti affect virtual all http relat middlewar refer for this issu includ http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"d2762ef7a24b09d4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32504341528608904, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17322797183727007, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67927945, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:25\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**svrnm** — 2025-11-18T07:54:04Z\\n\\n> When I read this proposal, I see this project as a an attempt to build a new registry (registry 2.0). I'm very supportive of this as I've been complaining about various deficiencies of the registry for some time.\\n\\nIt absolutely is! That's why I am in favour of this project so much. The registry has been a building block of our project from day 1, but besides a few cosmetic changes we never lifted it to a proper solution.\\n\\n> Significantly, the proposal is to launch the new effort in parallel to the existing registry, allowing the contributors to iterate quickly and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gathering.\\n\\nYes 🙌 \\n\\n> Later, once we've worked out the sharp edges, we can merge registry 1.0 into registry 2.0, and EOL registry 1.0.\\n\\nI can barely wait for it ;) \\n\\n>     * The registry already has a data model for capturing meta data about components (schema [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io?rgh-link-date=2025-11-10T15%3A29%3A30Z)), but its insufficient. As you note, there's all sorts of data which is important to capture and visualize for end users, which as of now, is very difficult for users to discover. The key examples being: configuration schema, schema of telemetry emitted, instructions on how to get started.\\n\\nYes, we can learn and take from the existing schema, but overall it's insufficient. \\n\\n>     * The [registry](https://opentelemetry.io/ecosystem/registry/) already has tools for searching for components, and displaying bits of information about them, but its insufficient. More than anything else, the registry is an index of links, requiring the user to follow the link and find installation / configuration / telemetry schema details in the linked website / repository. Except this information is no always available, and when it is, there's no standardization about the display. A richer registry schema would allow a richer / more useful visualization experience.\\n\\nThe registry as of today does what it was intended to do, provide a quick glance into all the things opentelemetry. but as the project evolved, the registry didn't, and as you lined out it's missing a lot of details and nuances, so this project aims to help with that. \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"svrnm 2025 11 18t07 54 04z when i read this propos i see this project a a an attempt to build a new registri registri 20 i m veri support of this a i ve been complain about various defici of the registri for some time it absolut is that s whi i am in favour of this project so much the registri ha been a build block of our project from day 1 but besid a few cosmet chang we never lift it to a proper solut signific the propos is to launch the new effort in parallel to the exist registri allow the contributor to iter quick and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gather yes later onc we ve work out the sharp edg we can merg registri 10 into registri 20 and eol registri 10i can bare wait for it the registri alreadi ha a data model for captur meta data about compon schema here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io rgh link date 2025 11 10t15 3a29 3a30z but it insuffici a you note there s all sort of data which is import to captur and visual for end user which a of now is veri difficult for user to discov the key exampl be configur schema schema of telemetri emit instruct on how to get start yes we can learn and take from the exist schema but overal it s insuffici the registri http opentelemetri io ecosystem registri alreadi ha tool for search for compon and display bit of inform about them but it insuffici more than anyth els the registri is an index of link requir the user to follow the link and find instal configur telemetri schema detail in the link websit repositori except this inform is no alway avail and when it is there s no standard about the display a richer registri schema would allow a richer more use visual experi the registri a of today doe what it wa intend to do provid a quick glanc into all the thing opentelemetri but a the project evolv the registri didn t and a you line out it s miss a lot of detail and nuanc so this project aim to help with that\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"54a7d35c2598fc15\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32406301196717147, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19232476281024496, \"vector_similarity\": 0.63145226, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**flc1125** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-11T13:20:30Z\\n\\n**flc1125** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\n**akats7** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\n**akats7** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/op